  "id": "rey-auditory-verbal-learning-test",
  "term": "Rey Auditory Verbal Learning Test",
  "definition": "The Rey Auditory Verbal Learning Test is a classic neuropsychological assessment that uses a spoken word list longer than immediate memory span to evaluate verbal memory and learning. It can provide scores for short-term recall, learning across repetitions, interference, and later retrieval such as delayed recall and recognition.",
